 abstract = {Advancements in information technology and the widespread use of the Internet have radically transformed global communication. Yet, these breakthroughs have also intensified challenges related to privacy and data security, particularly as sensitive information is exchanged across digital channels. In response, our research introduces a novel method that leverages artificial intelligence to conceal textual data within images, thereby enhancing security and confidentiality in digital communications. This study proposes an innovative approach where AI is employed to generate high-quality images from scratch, rather than relying on pre-existing cover images. These AI-generated images serve as secure carriers for encrypted messages, ensuring that the process not only maintains optimal image quality but also minimizes the risk of detection. A distinctive feature of our methodology is the application of RGB color masking, which preserves the visual integrity of the image while intricately embedding the hidden text. Moreover, our approach supports the encryption and concealment of Arabic text, broadening its applicability and reinforcing its relevance in diverse linguistic contexts. To evaluate the efficacy of our technique, we utilize rigorous quantitative measures such as distortion levels, accuracy of data retrieval, and detection rates. Preliminary results indicate that our method achieves superior speed, enhanced confidentiality, and significantly lower detectability when compared to traditional and modern techniques. Additionally, by integrating a mix of AI models, our approach optimizes the encryption and embedding processes, paving the way for more robust and versatile applications in digital security. Ultimately, this research not only addresses critical issues of data privacy and secure communication but also establishes a new paradigm in the field of steganography and encryption. By merging cutting-edge AI technology with advanced image processing techniques, our work lays the groundwork for more secure digital communication systems for digital security actors such as government agencies, schools, telecom providers, and messaging platforms can adopt the proposed methodology for integrating text hiding in different languages into AI-generated images, enabling a secure communication channel with high confidentiality and low vulnerability. This technology can also be easily integrated into existing encryption systems to enhance the protection of sensitive data without compromising image quality or network performance. And invites further exploration into innovative security solutions for the future.},
 author = {Atrash, Amr Jamal and Atawnih, Abdelrahem and Owda, Amani Yousef},
